---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Workflow from '../components/Workflow.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Laundry lockers for apartments & student housing | OurPort" description="Explore a wash-and-fold collection point for your apartment community or student residence. Plan resident access, laundry service and property needs together.">
  <section class="container housing-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">For apartments & student housing</p><h1>Laundry service, <br /> <span>closer to home.</span></h1><p class="lead">A familiar place to leave a laundry bag and collect it clean. A practical amenity, planned around your residents and their laundry provider.</p><a class="button" href="/plan-a-site/?role=housing">Plan your community’s service <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><figure><img src="/images/housing-lobby.webp" width="1672" height="941" alt="OurPort concept cabinet placed in a warm residential lobby beside the entrance." fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption>Residential lobby · illustrative concept</figcaption></figure></section>
  <section class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">An everyday amenity</p><h2>Less coordination. <br /> A more convenient routine.</h2></div><p>Connect a place residents already pass with a service they regularly need.</p></div><div class="three-columns"><article><h3>For your residents</h3><p>A consistent drop-off and return point, with access hours and pickup instructions agreed for the community.</p></article><article><h3>For your property team</h3><p>A workflow designed to keep routine bag handoffs with the resident and laundry provider, with a clear contact for exceptions.</p></article><article><h3>For your laundry provider</h3><p>A shared collection location and scheduled service route, with responsibility defined at each handoff.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="community-model"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">One location. Three coordinated roles.</p><h2>Useful to residents without becoming front-desk work.</h2></div><p>The operating model is settled with the property and laundry provider before launch.</p></div><div class="community-grid"><article><span>Resident</span><h3>A clear next step</h3><p>Know where to leave the bag, when the service accepts it, and when the finished order is ready.</p></article><article><span>Laundry provider</span><h3>A planned route and handoff</h3><p>Collect, accept, process and return orders under an agreed schedule and exception policy.</p></article><article><span>Property</span><h3>Defined boundaries</h3><p>Approve placement and access while the provider handles routine service and customer questions.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <Workflow housing />
  <section class="section container split-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your community. Your relationships.</p><h2>The property <br /> sets the ground rules.</h2><p>Placement, access, network use and any camera monitoring are coordinated with the property. Your resident relationship remains yours.</p><p>Already have a laundry provider or resident platform? We start there. Operator arrangements and system compatibility are reviewed for each location.</p></div><div class="review-list"><h3>A useful starting point</h3><ul><li>Number of homes or student beds</li><li>Current laundry service or provider search</li><li>Lobby or common-area placement</li><li>Resident and provider access</li><li>Network, monitoring and support ownership</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/plan-a-site/?role=housing">Share your site details <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="container property-checklist"><div><p class="eyebrow">What the property can expect to decide</p><h2>Five practical approvals.</h2></div><ol><li><span>01</span>Where the locker belongs</li><li><span>02</span>Who may access it, and when</li><li><span>03</span>Which network path is permitted</li><li><span>04</span>Whether monitoring is appropriate</li><li><span>05</span>Who owns exceptions and support</li></ol></section>
  <section class="container quiet-note"><p><strong>Start with laundry.</strong> Other service configurations can be considered as your property’s needs develop.</p></section>
  <section class="container housing-options"><div><p class="eyebrow">Optional site extensions</p><h2>Coordinate network and monitoring early.</h2></div><div><a href="/cctv/">Camera monitoring options <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/wifi-wap/">WiFi & WAP options <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  <CallToAction role="housing" title="Make room for a useful amenity." body="An existing community or a new development. Let’s look at the service, the space and the fit." />
</SiteLayout>
